// A correlation on the request's own caller -- `callerPrincipal: principal`.
//
// This is the ordinary way a policy says "the same principal did it", and until 2026-09-11 the
// vacuity checker CRASHED on it: its synthesized events carried no `session` field, which
// `BindHolds` reads for every scope bind, so TLC died with
//
//     Attempted to select nonexistent field "session" from the record
//
// Latent because no fixture used one -- every policy here joined on payload fields instead. It
// surfaced only when event schemas were wired in and a schema-shaped policy was tried.
//
// The expected answer is `live`: an Approve followed by a Trade, both by the same caller.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Anchor::Action::"Approve"::request{ callerPrincipal: principal }
};
